  "activity": {
    "id": "act_vectors_projectile",
    "name": "From Vectors to Projectile Motion",
    "description": "A hands-on AR progression that builds from abstract vector representation and addition, through component decomposition with right-triangle trigonometry, and applies these tools to understand two-dimensional projectile motion, the independence of horizontal and vertical motion, and how launch angle and speed shape the trajectory, range, and maximum height.",
    "language": "en",
    "workplace": "wp_vectors_projectile",
    "start": "step_intro_vectors",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "step_intro_vectors",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_01",
        "location": "vector_board",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "1. Vectors: Magnitude & Direction",
          "description": "Look at the Vector Workbench. A vector represents a quantity with both a magnitude (length of the arrow) and a direction (where it points). Observe the blue vector A displayed on the board, then say 'Next' to continue."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "vector_arrow_a",
              "poi": "board_center"
            },
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "info_label",
              "poi": "board_top",
              "text": "Vector A: magnitude = length, direction = where it points"
            },
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_intro",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_add_vectors",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_add_vectors",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_add_vectors",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_01",
        "location": "vector_board",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "2. Adding Vectors Tip-to-Tail",
          "description": "Now add two vectors. Vector B is placed with its tail at the tip of vector A. The red resultant vector runs from the tail of A to the tip of B. This tip-to-tail method gives the combined effect of both vectors. Click 'Next' when you understand the resultant."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "vector_arrow_a",
              "poi": "board_center"
            },
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "vector_arrow_b",
              "poi": "board_center"
            },
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "resultant_arrow",
              "poi": "board_center"
            },
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "info_label",
              "poi": "board_top",
              "text": "Resultant R = A + B (tail of A to tip of B)"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_decompose",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_decompose",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_decompose",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_01",
        "location": "vector_board",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "3. Components & Trigonometry",
          "description": "Point the Digital Protractor at vector A to reveal its components. The vector is decomposed into a horizontal (x) leg and a vertical (y) leg forming a right triangle. Use Ax = A\u00b7cos(theta) and Ay = A\u00b7sin(theta) to find the components, and A = sqrt(Ax^2 + Ay^2) to reconstruct the magnitude. Aim the protractor at the vector to continue."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "vector_arrow_a",
              "poi": "board_center"
            },
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "component_decomposition",
              "poi": "board_center"
            },
            {
              "target": "protractor_tool",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "trig_triangle_overlay",
              "poi": "pivot"
            },
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "info_label",
              "poi": "board_top",
              "text": "Ax = A cos(theta),  Ay = A sin(theta)"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "vector_board",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "protractor_tool",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "protractor_tool",
            "duration": 2000,
            "type": "tangible",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_launch_projectile",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_01",
        "location": "launch_pad",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "4. Launch a Projectile",
          "description": "Move to the Launch Pad. The launcher fires a projectile whose initial velocity is a vector, just like on the workbench. Watch the horizontal (constant) and vertical (changing) velocity components as the projectile follows its parabolic path. Aim the launcher and detect it to fire."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "launch_pad",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "parabola_trajectory",
              "poi": "muzzle"
            },
            {
              "target": "launcher_tool",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "velocity_components_anim",
              "poi": "angle_readout"
            },
            {
              "target": "trajectory_zone",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "gravity_arrow",
              "poi": "apex"
            },
            {
              "target": "launch_pad",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "info_label",
              "poi": "default",
              "text": "Initial velocity vector = horizontal + vertical components"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "launch_pad",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "launcher_tool",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "trajectory_zone",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "launcher_tool",
            "duration": 2000,
            "type": "tangible",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_independence",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_independence",
        "viewport": "reactions",
        "type": "reactions",
        "device": "hololens_01",
        "location": "trajectory_zone",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "5. Independence of Motion",
          "description": "Observe the key insight: the horizontal velocity stays constant (no horizontal force) while the vertical velocity decreases going up, reaches ZERO at maximum height, then increases downward. Horizontal and vertical motions are completely independent. The moment vertical velocity is zero marks the apex. Say 'Next' to explore range."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "trajectory_zone",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "velocity_components_anim",
              "poi": "apex"
            },
            {
              "target": "trajectory_zone",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "gravity_arrow",
              "poi": "apex"
            },
            {
              "target": "trajectory_zone",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_independence",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "trajectory_zone",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "info_label",
              "poi": "apex",
              "text": "At maximum height: vertical velocity = 0"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
